11. What Makes Wolfram QuantumFramework Unique: A Verified Showcase\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1540797058,ExpressionUUID->"00abf1cf-696b-3507-30a8-e8a9081f9c6d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Source: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"/", "Users"}], "/", "mohammadb"}], "/", "Documents"}], "/",
         "GitHub"}], "/", "QuantumFramework"}], "/", "OngoingProjects"}], "/",
      "Why"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"QF", "/", "QF"}]}], "-", 
   RowBox[{"Showcase", ".", "md"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03d898fe-d35a-9eef-31e7-11bbe6ece435"],
 " (examples run against the local QuantumFramework checkout)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->768596373,ExpressionUUID->"03dda600-4b0b-c3af-31e2-386a6ebf91f5"],

Cell["Summary", "Subsection",
 CellID->1985169054,ExpressionUUID->"4de38b79-ee67-8bee-7b90-23228b13d934"],

Cell["\<\
Seven claims, each argued by executed code: QF is symbolic-first; one object \
model spans channels, POVMs, Fock space and phase space; measurement records \
are quantum wires; three engines (state vector, tensor network, stabilizer \
tableau) compute the same objects; a QF object is an ordinary Wolfram \
Language expression; every object draws itself; and the same objects leave \
for OpenQASM, transpilers and IBM hardware. Each claim names its closest \
competitor and what remains distinctive.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->770675313,ExpressionUUID->"347cf1ed-0cc4-b4dc-5c03-e8b7a5761e26"],

Cell["What should catch a physicist's attention:", "Text",
 CellID->846554368,ExpressionUUID->"7d81b9ce-3a4c-aa2a-2bbe-30a8bffef970"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Time-ordered propagators in closed form.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A rotating-field qubit returns the lab-frame Rabi propagator; a \
Landau-Zener sweep returns a propagator in Kummer and parabolic-cylinder \
functions whose plot shows the Landau-Zener-St\[UDoubleDot]ckelberg \
oscillations the asymptotic formula ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "\[Pi]", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "2"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6bb9b374-9caf-337d-1946-2b3e155b9e47"],
 " misses."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1952818843,ExpressionUUID->"6c340229-13f4-0181-15cb-a473a58153eb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Exact variational landscapes.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " QAOA on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25dfa134-0866-9bb5-53e4-397ea910e99f"],
 ", built entirely from the graph, gives a closed-form energy surface whose \
maximum is a certified cubic root, below the true cut of 4."
}], "Item",
 CellID->599175116,ExpressionUUID->"425139cc-45a5-cefb-726e-b0966c5194c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["One master-equation solution for every qubit.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A symbolic density matrix and symbolic rates give the complete relaxation \
law at once, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], "\[LessEqual]", "2", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d922994-f334-45bb-7ba1-c0d186c12f81"],
 " comes out as a theorem via ",
 Cell[BoxData["Reduce"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06c25578-1780-b25e-2ef2-4d22a23a00a4"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1234886004,ExpressionUUID->"5f70617e-b140-9f95-0500-793bc0fae5ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Breadth in one object model.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Amplitude-damping purity loss ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79d0371a-30a6-04e5-2fef-af4441536ecf"],
 ", a tetrahedral SIC-POVM on a symbolic state, coherent-state dynamics as an \
identity in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d950d76-dd18-2b24-2baa-a533d4ad760e"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "2", 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7234a9f4-3232-6781-23cb-40be47c74deb"],
 " for Fock, coherent and thermal light, Wigner versus Husimi for a cat, \
exact zeros of multiphoton interference in Fourier multiports, a spin-1 NV \
Hamiltonian and a five-site ring diagonalized by named bases, and tomography \
from counts."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1955603644,ExpressionUUID->"42668d78-f434-72a4-721d-2525fdc1408e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Measurement without collapse.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Teleportation with its classical channel as record wires; a coherent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c7cc198-0ad8-2426-3403-d8c2af528f0c"],
 " error digitized into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69698b1d-3dc2-3628-1f16-2347b4749d72"],
 "/",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "701e1eb7-eeba-61c8-2025-97f08b4f3312"],
 " syndromes and corrected at fidelity exactly 1 for every input and angle; a \
measurement undone by its dilation's adjoint."
}], "Item",
 CellID->529524776,ExpressionUUID->"0e322415-281a-3695-37c1-be5f49ac9cff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Three engines, exact interconversion.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A Grover search contracted along a steered tensor-network path to an exact \
rational success probability; a 1000-qubit random Clifford state with an \
exact half-chain entropy; tableau, state vector and synthesized circuit \
agreeing under ",
 Cell[BoxData["SameQ"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "61beb272-ef15-9663-1745-343f8aa1fd49"],
 "; and a code layer returning a code's logical error rate as an exact \
polynomial in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e8a6a96-06b4-6465-0689-83d0b3414f4f"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->186212144,ExpressionUUID->"55951090-ef25-ccfd-03aa-89dd8ad196c7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Language-level operators.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData["Exp"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53a2ca13-da2c-324e-0151-ec5cdfde8094"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["D"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5930221d-821b-4026-08cf-c44737ae130c"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["Plus"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76ba63e9-5df8-c241-1e5a-7ab3547290ab"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["Commutator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "319e51f9-a9ce-1d21-67a6-48a2c87b640b"],
 " act on quantum objects; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], "."], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26f4962c-805e-a216-4e8b-087631e8f17c"],
 " recovers the drive of a target trajectory; a Werner-state criterion passed \
to ",
 Cell[BoxData["Reduce"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "313d5a7b-7caf-7acc-60c3-5c25755a4816"],
 " gives the exact entanglement threshold ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "<", "1", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2da78195-91be-94f0-5b5c-18df2048feda"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->284725946,ExpressionUUID->"39c6b7ab-78e0-e73c-6ffd-2ef5789aca06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Out to hardware.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " OpenQASM 3 export and import with exact angles (an imported CHSH circuit \
gives exactly the Tsirelson value), device transpilation, and a 4096-shot GHZ \
run on ",
 Cell[BoxData["ibm_fez"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f7d0c35-7157-44bf-6502-a67f00e22e85"],
 " drawn next to the exact distribution."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1006536905,ExpressionUUID->"47b49f91-c3c7-4deb-6d4b-16daf6721731"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["An honest boundary.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Closed forms stop where spectra stop being solvable in radicals \
(Abel-Ruffini), and QF signals it by returning ",
 Cell[BoxData["Root"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "064e3005-d89e-7c03-2e75-aa6ed92b4769"],
 " objects."
}], "Item",
 CellID->207506748,ExpressionUUID->"76c2caed-aea0-13a2-1ef1-e3b6cb556188"],

Cell["\<\
Example 11.1: the master equation solved once, for every qubit and every rate\
\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1146295856,ExpressionUUID->"260c3025-1fa9-9acd-4e33-a98f9a5de817"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "PacletDirectoryLoad", 
   "[", "\"\</Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/QuantumFramework/\
QuantumFramework\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$Assumptions", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Gamma]1", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Gamma]\[Phi]", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], " ", "&&", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"t", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Sigma]m", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]t", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]1", "]"}], " ", "\[Sigma]m"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]\[Phi]", "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     " ", "\[Rho]0", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", " ", "/@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]t", "[", "\"\<Computational\>\"", "]"}], 
     "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[68]:= ",
 CellID->438365529,ExpressionUUID->"4b1e6c2c-0452-4134-7925-8676ade7101e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every entry of the initial state stays a symbol: populations relax at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2982aea8-af87-65d7-5fb1-47f5ca324f3d"],
 ", coherences precess at ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19ac3a5e-0cd6-873c-4f53-bc18a560ea06"],
 " and decay at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "1"], "/", "2", "+", "2", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e8690e9-968f-68b3-16bd-09b3233a3a99"],
 ". The textbook bound between the two times is then a statement about all \
admissible rates:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->174000849,ExpressionUUID->"2b6bc1ec-c569-bd9f-5968-d8c9ec1d07e5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Reduce", "[", 
  RowBox[{"ForAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]1", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]\[Phi]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]1", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]\[Phi]", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"1", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Gamma]1", "/", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]\[Phi]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "<=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", "/", "\[Gamma]1"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[69]:= ",
 CellID->766726627,ExpressionUUID->"25f1a39a-81e0-db80-538e-3ac4379aa9ea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35466be2-b7a8-26dc-637d-82cfc2428c26"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], "\[LessEqual]", "2", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58bdea72-0ba3-5f4c-0842-0c3cae562596"],
 " is derived from the solution, not quoted, with equality exactly when pure \
dephasing vanishes."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1506609767,ExpressionUUID->"6e8cef58-e908-949c-16b3-070588a2fee6"],

Cell["\<\
Example 11.2: a coherent error, digitized and corrected, with measurement \
records as wires\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->281363281,ExpressionUUID->"0abc4047-6c7b-4886-3a44-5a21050e1aec"],

Cell["\<\
The parity measurements are degenerate projective measurements with two \
rank-two projectors; their outcomes land on record wires 0 and -1, and the \
corrections are gates controlled (and anti-controlled) on those records:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1615544595,ExpressionUUID->"24e21d63-fe6b-5877-4c91-954cfb1e2b5d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$Assumptions", " ", "=", " ", "True"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"id2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"zz", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"syn", "[", 
    RowBox[{"q1_", ",", " ", "q2_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
             RowBox[{"id2", ",", " ", "id2"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "zz"}], 
           ")"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"q1", ",", " ", "q2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
             RowBox[{"id2", ",", " ", "id2"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "zz"}], 
           ")"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"q1", ",", " ", "q2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"q1", ",", " ", "q2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"enc", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Label\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Encode\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qec", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"enc", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<RX\>\"", "[", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"syn", "[", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"syn", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<C\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<C\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<C\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "3"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"coded", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"qec", "[", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "\[Beta]"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<00\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[70]:= ",
 CellID->1805673747,ExpressionUUID->"348d2737-4aeb-e3cb-5cb2-bf716e9fb111"],

Cell["\<\
The joint distribution of the two syndrome records, for a symbolic data qubit \
and a symbolic error angle:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1547520620,ExpressionUUID->"2161c865-0900-0907-571e-e24fa8b5586d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"as", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Beta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Beta]", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Assuming", "[", 
  RowBox[{"as", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Diagonal", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
         RowBox[{"coded", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
        "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[71]:= ",
 CellID->858350929,ExpressionUUID->"3cadbe4b-a339-c651-6452-3014d6cdacbb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31169419-f57b-983b-672d-0e42fc0feb01"],
 ": the continuous rotation has become \"no error\" or \"qubit 2 flipped\", \
independent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40aa99e8-53bd-499c-70a9-10b266481be6"],
 ". After the feedforward, the data qubits match the ideal codeword:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2138894257,ExpressionUUID->"5d165407-aaf3-867b-0b2e-4e60ce87ed41"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Assuming", "[", 
  RowBox[{"as", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumSimilarity", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
        RowBox[{"coded", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"enc", "[", 
        RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "\[Beta]"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<00\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",",
        " ", "\"\<Fidelity\>\""}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[72]:= ",
 CellID->1941039383,ExpressionUUID->"75cb8946-a0dc-0da7-23c8-2123d169578d"],

Cell["\<\
Fidelity exactly 1 for every input and every angle: the digitization of \
errors, the founding theorem of quantum error correction, obtained from one \
symbolic run.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1670620029,ExpressionUUID->"63688a50-35e7-99e6-1117-2c1a4393ebcc"],

Cell["12. DRAG: Fast Gates on a Transmon", "Section",
 CellID->588214459,ExpressionUUID->"12187c95-2034-8b29-4238-75df51c6d673"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Source: ",
 Cell["\<\
/Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/QuantumFramework/QuantumFramework/\
Documentation/English/Tutorials/TransmonGates.md\
\>", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->"34b193bd-0a67-a7a6-5c4e-0ae7af130d8c"],
 " (the paclet tutorial, byte-identical to ",
 Cell["TransmonGatesV3.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "4fca8ec2-4b73-3b52-75c9-27ac6e0789b8"],
 ")."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1759496502,ExpressionUUID->"656925a1-dac3-d209-1316-bc0adf77a153"],

Cell["Summary", "Subsection",
 CellID->1641757231,ExpressionUUID->"09e13884-5cc5-f650-3f9e-b1ee5571dcba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How short can a \[Pi] pulse on a transmon be? A transmon is a weakly \
anharmonic oscillator, so a short, strong pulse leaks population into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29829495-262a-abaa-5fb1-0ddf53dcf9f0"],
 " and shifts the qubit transition away from the drive, while a long pulse \
suffers ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "136212ad-a4c2-b9f3-4111-8bf6cd740bd9"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67f6b273-a0bf-ee61-0d8d-343cd14bb54b"],
 ". The tutorial writes the driven anharmonic oscillator with a DRAG term in \
the rotating frame, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"\[Dagger]", "2"}]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
   FractionBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "."]}], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]], 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07a2a6c0-d7ac-3784-2d51-3fade25e9dee"],
 ", keeps five levels explicitly, and calibrates amplitude, detuning and DRAG \
coefficient together at every length under the Lindblad equation."
}], "Text",
 CellID->896279625,ExpressionUUID->"7d29df82-54ab-6c21-24d6-d6ec5d5e370b"],

Cell["What should catch a physicist's attention:", "Text",
 CellID->1264190945,ExpressionUUID->"2673b224-f5d9-a24c-4e00-2b81fc6df096"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Leakage seen directly.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " An uncalibrated 8 ns \[Pi] pulse at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "/", "2", "\[Pi]", "=", "-", "200"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27388ee6-22a7-f122-4ec7-27c05753c008"],
 " MHz leaves about a tenth of the population in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51cd4bfd-d3fa-9dcf-07f3-62a6e58ce715"],
 " and above; at 35 ns leakage is negligible but the flip is still incomplete \
because the drive shifts the qubit transition."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1806910998,ExpressionUUID->"06a776cb-b9d0-3c58-2e5d-6f95386a86a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["DRAG alone is not the answer.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Scanning ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7641b941-63e8-8619-1e7e-312b1582ed63"],
 " at fixed amplitude, leakage bottoms out near the weak-drive value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[TildeTilde]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42b8cf72-fa81-ffe6-7247-e73fff35c5cc"],
 ", but the transfer error is smallest at a much smaller ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c8db7a0-3aa3-299f-44b2-2e0abf567be5"],
 ": the leftover error is population still in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "473593be-64fb-e664-6eca-0af80c8fcd4e"],
 ". Amplitude, detuning and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79a8e286-b760-8808-2f57-fbe3c21adb52"],
 " must be calibrated together."
}], "Item",
 CellID->962064851,ExpressionUUID->"766f3dde-6e6e-8ae3-1e14-b4980b18d8c9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The speed limit is set by decoherence, not leakage.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Calibrated under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], "=", "100", "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7acff19c-f8f8-c05b-2af4-e8d9f97292a1"],
 "s, the DRAG curve turns up at a much shorter length and reaches a lower \
minimum than the plain pulse; at the optimum both errors are dominated by \
decay and dephasing, and DRAG wins by being shorter. A narrow dip near 10 ns \
echoes Da Costa Jesus et al. (2025)."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1660212291,ExpressionUUID->"36bb0aa4-099e-3511-5e58-a30ea8289c7b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The model checks itself.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The gate error averaged over six input states stays close to the transfer \
error (time-reversal symmetry of the pulse), and three levels underestimate \
leakage while five and six agree."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1553450743,ExpressionUUID->"6fab4322-7f5b-c123-15a9-5a8c7aef9009"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["All in one object.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", "5", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "559c0528-76f1-864e-03a3-9d720285ec94"],
 ", a parametrized ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c3b3e9a-7f95-6e09-75d8-b7c47a203553"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b834648-1855-f17e-29b1-581299e1c044"],
 " for both Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger and Lindblad dynamics, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<ReturnEquations\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6aa15cf4-f328-f435-1a5f-55b186c2df1f"],
 " to hand the 25 density-matrix equations to ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolveValue"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1fa3178e-7287-38be-4550-8ee807338a84"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["NMinimize"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33c53063-afff-c489-61fa-aa4cc98baed3"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->376345483,ExpressionUUID->"08d8bcb3-70a4-55b3-38e7-35fd01513f99"],

Cell["Example 12.1: leakage, and what DRAG does to it", "Subsection",
 CellID->1917523023,ExpressionUUID->"20e38226-5aed-155d-5090-1b805e987fa7"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "PacletDirectoryLoad", 
   "[", "\"\</Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/QuantumFramework/\
QuantumFramework\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], ";", " ", 
  
  RowBox[{
  "Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"", "]"}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"envelope", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"A", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "\[Tau]"}], ")"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", 
        RowBox[{"t", "/", "\[Tau]"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"hamiltonian", "[", "c_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"c", " ", "@", " ", "c"}]}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Delta]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", "c"}], 
      ")"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"envelope", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"c", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"D", "[", 
         RowBox[{"envelope", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Alpha]"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "c"}], 
        ")"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"anharmonicity", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "Pi", " ", "0.2"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"finalPopulations", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "amplitude_", ",", " ", "drag_", ",", " ", "detuning_", ",", " ", 
       "length_"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"hamiltonian", "[", 
           RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", "n", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
            "\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "A", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", 
             "\[Delta]", ",", " ", "\[Tau]"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "[", "\n", 
        "    ", 
        RowBox[{
        "anharmonicity", ",", " ", "amplitude", ",", " ", "drag", ",", " ", 
         "detuning", ",", " ", "length"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "length"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<ExplicitRungeKutta\>\""}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"PrecisionGoal", " ", "->", " ", "12"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"AccuracyGoal", " ", "->", " ", "14"}]}], "]"}], "[", "length",
      "]"}], "[", "\n", "  ", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[73]:= ",
 CellID->225924774,ExpressionUUID->"160727ef-d1b8-0069-3e3c-bec8e04d52b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The populations of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Ket"], ",", 
   TemplateBox[{"1"},
    "Ket"], ",", 
   TemplateBox[{"2"},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "261df1b1-b81e-57af-4e22-e8fb39ab3df5"],
 " after an uncalibrated \[Pi] pulse of 8 ns and of 35 ns:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1508526016,ExpressionUUID->"00ba9d2f-c328-50fc-3059-1488f6dd22c6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"finalPopulations", "[", 
     RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], 
     "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{";;", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"finalPopulations", "[", 
     RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "35"}], "}"}]}], 
     "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{";;", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[74]:= ",
 CellID->1653333794,ExpressionUUID->"02964792-f196-8b6e-32ae-5edf8020d9b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At 8 ns roughly a tenth of the population has left the qubit; at 35 ns \
leakage is gone but a fraction of a percent stays in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166d4e5f-4333-9385-3e13-601976c7e1ef"],
 ". Now scan the DRAG coefficient at 8 ns and compare leakage with transfer \
error:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2117504204,ExpressionUUID->"1c99ee20-d785-d362-44a6-078de231be48"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLogPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"With", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"finalPopulations", "[", 
           RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "drag", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "8"}], 
             "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"drag", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
             RowBox[{"p", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"3", " ", ";;"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"drag", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{"p", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"drag", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "0.1"}], 
       "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Joined", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotMarkers", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<leakage\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<transfer error\>\""}], "}"}]}],
    ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[Lambda]\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<population\>\""}], "}"}]}]}],
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[75]:= ",
 CellID->201091240,ExpressionUUID->"60858f89-56d8-6615-10ba-26d3636d4d7f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Leakage is minimized near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[TildeTilde]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e45545e-c429-efe4-567b-4e1bedddb5ce"],
 ", the weak-drive value, but the transfer error is minimized well below it: \
suppressing leakage and completing the flip are different targets. And the \
truncation is safe:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->667003370,ExpressionUUID->"24564246-a2b2-7a9b-4c6e-6423d74748e1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"finalPopulations", "[", 
        RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}],
         "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"3", " ", ";;"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[76]:= ",
 CellID->526043023,ExpressionUUID->"273d1382-afb1-09c0-4ec2-8aefca445b2a"],

Cell["\<\
Three levels miss about half the leakage; five and six agree.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1120596176,ExpressionUUID->"39c9e52f-ed06-87fb-6ff6-fc8884b0edc1"],

Cell["\<\
Example 12.2: calibrating the 8 ns pulse, with and without DRAG\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->64105026,ExpressionUUID->"46be6341-4be3-06d9-6e46-7b2b6d966c23"],

Cell["\<\
Minimize the transfer error over amplitude and detuning, and over the DRAG \
coefficient as well (closed system, a quick differential-evolution search):\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1373525465,ExpressionUUID->"352b8971-1d3f-d4c9-6328-213b94cbbe13"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"err", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"l_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"d_", "?", "NumericQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"finalPopulations", "[", 
      RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "l", ",", " ", "d", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], 
      "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"NMinimize", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"err", "[", 
        RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "d"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "a", " ", "<", " ", "2"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "0.5"}], " ", "<=", " ", "d", " ", "<=", " ", 
         "0.5"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "0.8", ",", " ", "1.2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "0.1"}], ",", " ", "0.1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<DifferentialEvolution\>\"", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<SearchPoints\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "10"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<RandomSeed\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
    "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"NMinimize", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"err", "[", 
        RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "l", ",", " ", "d"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "a", " ", "<", " ", "2"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
        RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "l", " ", "<=", " ", "3"}], " ", "&&", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "0.5"}], " ", "<=", " ", "d", " ", "<=", " ", 
         "0.5"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "0.8", ",", " ", "1.2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"l", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "0.1"}], ",", " ", "0.1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<DifferentialEvolution\>\"", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<SearchPoints\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "10"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<RandomSeed\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[77]:= ",
 CellID->1964307623,ExpressionUUID->"227c7e4b-1c68-aac8-5204-70159502f812"],

Cell["\<\
This search takes about five minutes, and even so it is coarse; it still \
shows the mechanism: with only amplitude and detuning the 8 ns pulse cannot \
get below the percent level, while adding the DRAG coefficient cuts the error \
several-fold, with a nonzero detuning compensating the drive-induced shift. \
The tutorial's full scan repeats this under the Lindblad equation from 6 to \
40 ns (the longest computation in the tutorial, run in parallel) to find \
where decoherence takes over.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->39040159,ExpressionUUID->"6cd9b5a9-dbed-51da-14e6-2cf2dd982320"],

Cell["13. QuantumInterferometer: Symbolic Behaviour", "Section",
 CellID->1242473813,ExpressionUUID->"4becebe3-5bfe-fac0-7993-02cd5d88c82a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Source: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"/", "Users"}], "/", "mohammadb"}], "/", "Documents"}], "/",
         "GitHub"}], "/", "QuantumFramework"}], "/", "OngoingProjects"}], "/",
      "Quantum"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Interferometer", "/", "QI"}]}], "-", "symbolic", "-", 
   RowBox[{"showcase", ".", "md"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "312d182f-c6c7-5e1e-60d2-9188f3722564"],
 " (a reference page of input/output pairs rather than an essay; ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumInterferometer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1449d45f-8382-90b9-3c76-ce193634e283"],
 " lives in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`", "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->"444f09dd-766a-dba7-6c74-a087031ca98d"],
 " context, which must be loaded)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->290269587,ExpressionUUID->"79e9b65a-67eb-1624-2f96-2804119e7d0e"],

Cell["Summary", "Subsection",
 CellID->471335900,ExpressionUUID->"394df0e2-3b3f-7a44-6f72-e9ccbeca48ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumInterferometer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d3de1d4-e864-19c9-04c2-f89189116b13"],
 " is QF's linear-optics object: beam splitters, phase shifters, squeezers \
and loss acting on Fock, coherent and squeezed light. This page catalogues \
what it does when the inputs are symbols, angles, amplitudes, squeezing \
parameters, loss rates, and above all photon numbers."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1843091513,ExpressionUUID->"1adc8861-0296-99d3-4ae3-224bb720eb39"],

Cell["What should catch a physicist's attention:", "Text",
 CellID->1978684664,ExpressionUUID->"47f3727e-1788-b883-6d81-7438a2220ae9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Symbolic photon numbers.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A beam splitter's amplitude from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02bfa0ec-e0fe-2fa7-3244-39c9908b758d"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7cc1833e-1ead-5711-24fe-1b789b583a7b"],
 " comes back as a Wigner ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3cb4236e-91b2-9328-644b-bb482044fe72"],
 "-function times a Kronecker delta for photon conservation (the Schwinger \
two-mode realization of SU(2)), for symbolic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "631da35c-735e-7e3b-1122-3b0606eb4501"],
 ". Chains of splitters return held sums over internal photon numbers with \
the right bounds, and path conditions appear as ",
 Cell[BoxData["Piecewise"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "44b7daea-ed84-b50e-6c4c-d3b784361c54"],
 " only when photon flow does not imply them."
}], "Item",
 CellID->2064137570,ExpressionUUID->"39f2334d-24de-3dcb-6f81-ab174d688711"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Hong-Ou-Mandel for every ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"1ec600b7-0050-8550-46fd-99f1b1eaefba"],
 StyleBox[".",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " On a balanced splitter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]},
    "Ket"], "\[Rule]", 
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], ",", "2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33bfe66e-cd59-d601-6144-f84be4edbd6b"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["k", "TI"], "-", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a3ee8c1-8740-e1ad-1bc5-01ab32fab3f7"],
 ", and every odd split vanishes."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1265784226,ExpressionUUID->"33885b0f-111a-0c54-6188-5369a0af56be"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Coherent, squeezed and lossy light, exactly.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Coherent states map to coherent states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], "\[Rule]", 
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c9080a8-67dd-9047-04af-19f21269e2ad"],
 "; squeezed-vacuum photon statistics come out as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["sech",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["tanh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2abc9d06-0494-496b-5a43-1560ad211bb1"],
 " series; two squeezers on a splitter cancel coincidences for equal \
squeezing and maximize them for opposite squeezing (a two-mode squeezed \
vacuum); loss gives the binomial law ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
    "Binomial"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"1", "-", 
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43e301a0-76bb-1057-7190-980a034e62bd"],
 " for symbolic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ae06f2b-7109-3ba5-4a9f-877500bd898f"],
 ", multiplicative rates on one mode, and coherences scaled by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0856a555-3f58-6085-386d-3d1fbaed32ef"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->872599864,ExpressionUUID->"71eecbe3-9be0-9ba6-2795-e2cd1d9ae98c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A physical-domain contract.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Photon numbers are nonnegative integers, angles real, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "\[LessEqual]", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "\[LessEqual]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "59070895-187c-42ea-0f3c-a1df99091030"],
 "; results carry no conditions restating that domain, user assumptions \
refine them, and contradictory assumptions fail rather than return nonsense."
}], "Item",
 CellID->2056057710,ExpressionUUID->"189fe470-6cd8-7cf4-48a4-fe3a056d46de"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Stated limits.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Section 8 lists precisely what is not supported symbolically, and the \
final section records the gaps found while running the list (substitute \
photon numbers before machine-number angles, which ",
 Cell[BoxData["Refine"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04ed2843-d86c-272a-2c92-c22cd91e8a70"],
 " simplifications are left to the caller)."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1360523735,ExpressionUUID->"70d9e217-b7c7-416b-20e6-0450c27213b1"],

Cell["\<\
Example 13.1: a beam splitter with symbolic photon numbers, and \
Hong-Ou-Mandel for every n\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->676766013,ExpressionUUID->"29221b72-bc55-8ef4-58d1-933c35e1d4de"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "PacletDirectoryLoad", 
   "[", "\"\</Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/QuantumFramework/\
QuantumFramework\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], ";", " ", 
  
  RowBox[{
  "Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"", "]"}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"th", ",", " ", "ph"}], "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"bs", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"n1", ",", " ", "n2"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t1", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"n1", " ", "+", " ", "n2", " ", "-", " ", "t1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[78]:= ",
 CellID->1428640414,ExpressionUUID->"41172bde-c012-830e-772c-c29bf1a4ee54"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The amplitude is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], "-", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}], ",", "\[ThickSpace]", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], "-", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "/", "2"}]}]}], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]}]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3dd84232-0c35-660d-6bf8-647ca5c04d57"],
 ": a two-mode beam splitter is a rotation of a spin of size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5558c8fc-3d33-9e90-0367-e1a6b4c7e4fa"],
 ", and the photon numbers are its magnetic quantum numbers. On a balanced \
splitter with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53291d47-a111-bd44-02d6-9520d0a507ae"],
 " photons in each port:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1143649234,ExpressionUUID->"14460f59-6b0f-818e-3c7d-a7030ebbd3d4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hom", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], "}"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], " ", "-", " ", "k"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"hom", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"hom", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"n", " ", "->", " ", "m"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"k", " ", "->", " ", "j"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"m", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "m"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "2"}], 
      "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"hom", " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"n", " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"k", " ", "->", " ", "j"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[79]:= ",
 CellID->1571962290,ExpressionUUID->"6afe19ed-5a5e-331e-1a85-90b75fe89e64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One formula for all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "142f588d-e120-bc70-3dd5-51d690da075a"],
 "; every odd split is exactly zero (the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "029948d8-232c-2201-32a7-618256d9716b"],
 " case is the Hong-Ou-Mandel dip), and for two photons per port the outputs \
are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "3", "/", "8"}], ",", "0", ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ",", "0", ",", 
   RowBox[{"3", "/", "8", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b1b5b6f-b43d-594b-7939-53493dc82b91"],
 ". Chaining two splitters gives a held sum over the internal photon number \
that, once activated, agrees with the concrete query:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2091585593,ExpressionUUID->"32f703b9-71e1-95eb-628c-9ae30795ff31"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"chain", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"th1", ",", " ", "ph1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"th2", ",", " ", "ph2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Activate", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"chain", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"n", " ", "-", " ", "t"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "/.", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"n", " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"t", " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{"chain", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[80]:= ",
 CellID->30157833,ExpressionUUID->"0c860bbc-8d1f-f590-34bd-a2e624abdffa"],

Cell["\<\
Example 13.2: loss, squeezing and coherent light in closed form\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1715653387,ExpressionUUID->"1bab88a0-6539-d521-49a8-210a0ccdbc0b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Loss on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74b37722-3fdc-1a4f-1c41-6e8cba696895"],
 " photons, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31781dc2-1028-33d4-6707-94aca1c2813e"],
 " symbolic, and a coherent pair through a general splitter:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1904268993,ExpressionUUID->"2148b02c-d62e-5336-5777-2989e3db3e1c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Loss\>\"", "[", "eta", "]"}], "}"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "n", "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "k", "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"bs", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b"}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[81]:= ",
 CellID->1610510011,ExpressionUUID->"183293a6-0d60-7813-49c1-0a00a4154b79"],

Cell["\<\
The binomial loss law, and a coherent state that stays coherent with \
amplitudes rotated by the transfer matrix. Two squeezed vacua meeting on a \
balanced splitter, and the photon statistics of one squeezed vacuum:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1363210520,ExpressionUUID->"61e1f3c1-eae0-3799-179e-eaaa8e9a9de3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", "x1", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", "x2", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", "xi", "]"}], "}"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Cutoff\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "4"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"xi", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[82]:= ",
 CellID->751311520,ExpressionUUID->"20bddc2d-650e-8031-5042-d6770cb8d31b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The coincidence amplitude is proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["arg",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"]}]], 
   StyleBox["tanh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["arg",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"]}]], 
   StyleBox["tanh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a437910-f355-55ba-2a71-715d86e03f80"],
 ": it vanishes for equal squeezing, where the output is two independent \
squeezed vacua, and is largest for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], "=", "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49429438-4a3e-974e-7f71-0e626fc8fd94"],
 ", where the splitter makes a two-mode squeezed vacuum. The squeezed vacuum \
populates only even photon numbers, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["sech",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07e2168c-1726-1a27-2d91-8fd6a2d3690d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["sech",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["tanh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3540c51c-f580-c338-637f-dd59fc3aae02"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["3", "8"], 
   StyleBox["sech",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["tanh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "684f0173-fe99-1571-1874-993cfb2c7c5b"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1811324800,ExpressionUUID->"6e32c5a8-aee9-5273-17c1-dcf5ca9c2159"],

Cell["14. Quantum Optics with QuantumInterferometer", "Section",
 CellID->1255352889,ExpressionUUID->"607492e2-157b-ba0c-100b-0bcc9c0f0956"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Source: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"/", "Users"}], "/", "mohammadb"}], "/", "Documents"}], "/",
         "GitHub"}], "/", "QuantumFramework"}], "/", "OngoingProjects"}], "/",
      "Quantum"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Interferometer", "/", "interferometer"}]}], "-", 
   RowBox[{"showcase", ".", "md"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7781757c-388d-abb9-1dbf-6d26b939f983"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1056550259,ExpressionUUID->"566e7348-207a-dc95-7e16-6b12510ca6ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Note for review: the closing \"Scope\" section and section 11 say lossy \
sampling is unsupported and that ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Samples\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39672ae7-82f4-b353-6f1c-c3c1368601b9"],
 "/",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<SampleCounts\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c48aba4-6f27-6a39-3477-420e0ad23903"],
 " support only lossless passive networks. On the current kernel (after \
commits c91ca9ad and 24f5679f, \"lossy and coherent samples\") a lossy \
network samples without complaint, for example ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<Loss\>\"", "[", "0.5", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}], 
     "}"}], "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<SampleCounts\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "1000"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f62374d-f3df-131c-5511-af16866a7e66"],
 " returns counts; those two sentences look stale."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1554899303,ExpressionUUID->"455ea632-3d4d-f0d3-7365-387cb4f9c239"],

Cell["Summary", "Subsection",
 CellID->1285549060,ExpressionUUID->"1f0fb95c-030e-c889-4534-3106b6b89ad3"],

Cell["\<\
Fourteen linear-optics experiments, each ending in a checked prediction: \
Hong-Ou-Mandel, Reck/Clements/cosine-sine meshes, Fourier multiports, \
squeezed light and Gaussian boson sampling, Mach-Zehnder fringes, coherent \
states and dark ports, twin-Fock interference, tunable four-photon \
suppression, heralded state preparation, multiphoton fringes, disentangling \
squeezers and Bloch-Messiah forms, pure loss, waveguide arrays and quantum \
walks, and the KLM nonlinear sign gate. Fock amplitudes are permanents, \
squeezed amplitudes hafnians, and loss acts on probabilities and finite \
states directly.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1616846310,ExpressionUUID->"16268eae-a572-7912-3fdd-270bcc074878"],

Cell["What should catch a physicist's attention:", "Text",
 CellID->1706199142,ExpressionUUID->"346a0e1a-2221-987e-5c69-a04457d5eb44"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Exact zeros are the signal.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " HOM's coincidence is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "366be24c-537a-43bb-5e68-0416660f1181"],
 "; a Fourier tritter forbids every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "2"}], ",", "1", ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "501b1457-1a1d-907b-0038-8e119fa9e341"],
 " pattern; with four modes 25 of 35 patterns vanish exactly, which floating \
point would blur."
}], "Item",
 CellID->848974671,ExpressionUUID->"291c68e0-f532-6cdd-5f23-81cdfcc73627"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Laws for every photon number.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Twin-Fock inputs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c29c458-c353-7b98-05d6-de05f6e649e2"],
 " never give odd outputs, explained by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2", "2"], "-", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["z", "TI"], "1", "2"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e1a2d6a-d2ad-c32a-1639-c537e759ae70"],
 " and closed as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
    "Binomial"], 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{"2", 
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "2", 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], 
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]},
     "Binomial"], "/", 
    SuperscriptBox["4", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6eb5612b-2266-f0f1-164b-79755710c2db"],
 ", normalized by ",
 Cell[BoxData["Sum"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f4b4965-e043-b514-4549-614e91f71c7e"],
 " for all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bf36e21-2d79-2b6f-0980-878b440c79b5"],
 "; pure loss is binomial for symbolic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fe9f85b-1ce6-27f0-1596-f20594908dda"],
 " with mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"n", "\[Eta]"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3eadea9f-7d43-757d-6652-03d974f65c47"],
 " proved by summation."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1375299215,ExpressionUUID->"68be2dd2-eea3-f2cb-1845-c49f8b57c011"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Tunable suppression.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"2,2"},
    "Ket"], "\[Rule]", 
   TemplateBox[{"2,2"},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1279eb8d-ef8a-5dbb-4206-02d68a3f2781"],
 " has amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "-", "6", 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6afb4307-9f81-9d1b-1a99-5b611a35e461"],
 ", so it vanishes at the two unbalanced reflectivities ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"3", "\[PlusMinus]", 
    SqrtBox["3"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e902be9-4fb4-3e90-56af-c2b36a4684fa"],
 ", and the zeros move with photon number."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1656178105,ExpressionUUID->"46e8ad28-93a4-355d-6e97-457226569fa7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Squeezed light, symbolically.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Opposite squeezers on a balanced splitter give a two-mode squeezed vacuum \
with geometric pair law ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["tanh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cosh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43090fa7-5002-8b65-7136-a60161b4d64f"],
 "; undoing the splitter returns two independent squeezed vacua exactly; a \
four-mode hafnian amplitude matches a six-level Fock-space circuit to machine \
precision."
}], "Item",
 CellID->2128368636,ExpressionUUID->"0d6689b0-bbf9-a698-3b1d-20fa3d8d0ce2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Heralding and gates.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A photon plus weak coherent light, conditioned on one detected photon, \
approximates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"], "-", 
     TemplateBox[{"1"},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ac87485-b214-a6e0-7ac8-6deec7a60cca"],
 "; the KLM nonlinear sign gate built from a three-mode real unitary gives \
amplitudes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", "1", ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1", "}", "/", "2"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e1d4b5-6b25-2976-7e9e-cdff0ed0785c"],
 " on signal photon numbers 0, 1, 2, success probability exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e41722a-1026-02f0-567f-7474a1d350da"],
 " for every input, and a different amplitude at three photons, where the \
gate is undefined."
}], "Item",
 CellID->471452856,ExpressionUUID->"6aacec8a-85e6-bbaa-1a53-05d4339009f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cross-checks everywhere.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Permanents against Fock-space circuits, native loss against a vacuum-mode \
dilation, waveguide propagators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c51a735-fee5-6802-446e-3f7efa903b68"],
 " against beam-splitter meshes, sample frequencies against exact \
distributions, a discrete-time quantum walk against the classical binomial \
walk."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1993504316,ExpressionUUID->"5e54a15d-ecde-9aa9-066b-39068568e8f3"],

Cell["Example 14.1: the KLM nonlinear sign gate, exactly", "Subsection",
 CellID->1944276818,ExpressionUUID->"27fb6428-ecec-27d4-4d99-7e75849e8d3e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A three-mode real unitary with one auxiliary photon; success is heralded by \
the auxiliary pattern ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51f5ca74-88a2-9d2c-078a-ec3e2954e476"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->524220529,ExpressionUUID->"1154648e-ef0b-aa2b-476c-7deb8abff971"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "PacletDirectoryLoad", 
   "[", "\"\</Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/QuantumFramework/\
QuantumFramework\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], ";", " ", 
  
  RowBox[{
  "Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"", "]"}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nsMatrix", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", "^", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "4"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"3", "/", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", "^", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "4"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"3", "/", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nsGate", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", "nsMatrix", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"RootReduce", "[", 
     RowBox[{"nsMatrix", " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "nsMatrix", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"RootReduce", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"nsGate", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
         
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[83]:= ",
 CellID->950216136,ExpressionUUID->"4c057904-8649-af2b-743b-716e33fdf271"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The heralded amplitudes for 0, 1 and 2 signal photons are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], ",", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2baf9433-2e90-ebaf-5954-0e7d4b2ab9f5"],
 ": a sign flip on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "340e6ec8-e38f-b030-5c35-8795963b031a"],
 " alone, which no phase shifter can do, with success probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64bff79f-1679-3ebc-0c44-eed9a30d8486"],
 " independent of the input. The three-photon amplitude, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    SqrtBox["2"], "-", "5"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "126dc52b-3dd5-bd31-4212-dd75b461041b"],
 ", shows where the gate's domain ends."
}], "Text",
 CellID->338647958,ExpressionUUID->"28023c0b-10a3-7000-5831-b655a156436a"],

Cell["\<\
Example 14.2: squeezed pairs and tunable four-photon suppression\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->961910044,ExpressionUUID->"4f1b960d-0301-b7cd-7538-0857b6b51d17"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Opposite single-mode squeezers and a balanced splitter, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "268b8fe7-2cf2-fa64-4e88-26c14484c94e"],
 " symbolic:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1465513701,ExpressionUUID->"41763b34-5a53-ec31-770d-b37e5fe7b71b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"symbolicPair", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", "r", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", 
        RowBox[{"-", "r"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"symbolicPair", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"r", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"symbolicPair", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"r", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[84]:= ",
 CellID->1779278278,ExpressionUUID->"5d61c4f4-c0fb-847a-0b1e-ddb1f08fef40"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Photons come only in pairs across the two modes, with the geometric law ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sech",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["tanh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72fe9a0c-0c49-239f-2285-1c56a5fc71e5"],
 ", and unequal patterns are exactly zero: a two-mode squeezed vacuum. Now \
the return amplitude of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2,2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14bcbead-0cb8-f132-3c43-37f7a532c018"],
 " on a beam splitter of angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a015340-38cc-91ca-7a3f-4b2ab97ee310"],
 ", and the reflectivities that kill it:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->332869652,ExpressionUUID->"44807b7f-366d-41a7-6cb0-73394318138d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fourBS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fa", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"fourBS", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"fa", " ", "==", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"6", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"R", " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"6", " ", "R", " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "R"}], ")"}]}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
        "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "R", " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}], ",", " ", "R",
       ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[85]:= ",
 CellID->870462011,ExpressionUUID->"56b5d630-2397-dc8b-7e4a-c87a5623a6d1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The amplitude is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "-", "6", 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "066e8396-42fa-b64f-2e15-1ad0768c1c95"],
 ", zero at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"3", "\[PlusMinus]", 
    SqrtBox["3"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0fee4e15-659c-ade9-3596-605f0c2ef733"],
 ": unlike HOM, four-photon cancellation needs an unbalanced splitter, and \
the two settings are mirror images under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], "\[LeftRightArrow]", "1", "-", 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f99faa1-7599-adaa-15a6-f30b7c2df7f0"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->770594293,ExpressionUUID->"6c80f068-193e-1d5a-14bf-ea3298cb67a0"],

Cell["15. A Formal Semantics for QuantumFramework", "Section",
 CellID->416617480,ExpressionUUID->"77601adb-bf25-4789-1d1f-93853ad02dd3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Source: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"/", "Users"}], "/", "mohammadb"}], "/", "Documents"}], "/",
         "GitHub"}], "/", "QuantumFramework"}], "/", "OngoingProjects"}], "/",
      "Formal"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Semantics", "/", "QF"}]}], "-", "formal", "-", 
   RowBox[{"semantics", ".", "md"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48b830c7-d270-6a57-7847-a9a0e70538bd"],
 " (written against QF 2.1.1, kernel ",
 Cell[BoxData["b13a9077"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62f1d7f5-6807-0c72-128e-cebf09b25758"],
 "; its ",
 Cell[".nb", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "1e2af966-75ba-f15e-4629-f1407c4cc3a4"],
 " predates the latest text edits)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->468951994,ExpressionUUID->"7fcb302b-9e92-9019-25c8-aa751b24e363"],

Cell["Summary", "Subsection",
 CellID->1802328397,ExpressionUUID->"361ba0ac-b25b-03c3-5e38-3909c7ee5129"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "What does a QF object ",
 StyleBox["mean", "TI"],
 "? The document answers object by object: what QF stores, and what it does \
with what it stores when it applies, composes, tensors, adjoints, discards, \
measures and evolves. The single thread is that a coefficient array means \
nothing until its subsystem dimensions, its output/input split and its bases \
are fixed, and QF stores exactly those. One running example, the operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c5768f-9366-0c29-5efb-6fe926135773"],
 " whose stored coefficients are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fcd6d4-594a-1482-7183-cf9e58ff7ee8"],
 " in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4719bc21-ede2-73f0-6d26-358a8b9741da"],
 " basis (so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71a147e0-ad25-39c0-275f-5ecdc4d18b2a"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["is", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d94734f-f5fd-5b1e-3bac-6b2883882664"],
 "), carries every section."
}], "Text",
 CellID->328865975,ExpressionUUID->"4a66d044-93ea-cfa5-7a1d-ca2e259c958f"],

Cell["What should catch a physicist's attention:", "Text",
 CellID->1270006433,ExpressionUUID->"08e3a6ae-198b-2f89-3890-3f08983e75d3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Numbers versus maps.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Six numbers can be a six-level qudit, a qubit and a qutrit, or a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07ff9e3d-196e-b566-2d84-106798181c4c"],
 " map such as photon subtraction; the stored matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7611561e-6aa4-cbf1-1e2f-48580f5699db"],
 " and the represented map ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d91ad73-9dce-768e-1bae-453d147b5cd4"],
 " are related by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"o", "u", "t"}], "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"i", "n"}], "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6bff65fb-5d0a-196c-1985-7ca554bf6bb6"],
 " for any invertible (not necessarily orthonormal) basis."
}], "Item",
 CellID->34003199,ExpressionUUID->"5e58ca76-8595-5ac4-0667-ec302c20282e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why bases must be reconciled before composing.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Composing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08a91809-3406-7705-3856-9253bdb35a6f"],
 " after ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47ee4125-d524-d464-6d96-588edcd6bf4e"],
 " by contracting the stored numbers would give the identity; QF changes \
coordinates first and returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Z", "X"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a0bea5a-c3ff-c671-4a08-0c07f58bad5b"],
 ". The correctness requirement for composition is stated as a theorem about \
computational matrices."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1596250240,ExpressionUUID->"2d2ec88d-5e53-28f6-54d5-e1d75be67adc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["One operator-space model for channels, evolution and phase space.",
  
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Vectorization turns maps on density matrices into ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "230fc3bf-d3e5-5aa5-5134-daf8e590288f"],
 "s on the operator space (",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Left\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c6e076f-8b93-3c10-3415-9f492e27877a"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Right\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29094997-c9cb-f733-5f37-60d0e87fda19"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Liouvillian\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "284fc6fb-b6ce-6422-5874-dfa4c37b4f08"],
 "); a channel is stored as a Stinespring isometry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]},
      "Ket"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cad16aa-0a89-b805-3452-8ff4af3d0b6f"],
 "; the phase-space picture is a change of coordinates of the same matrices, \
so it preserves composition."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1572158672,ExpressionUUID->"5640583a-c911-1fe8-7e70-5267e8a46532"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["One isometry, three readings.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The extra index of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6944803a-8297-e066-1f7b-1a643723b34c"],
 " can be kept as a live wire (coherent branches), traced (the channel) or \
read (the measurement); and the same list of matrices means Kraus operators \
to ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumChannel"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9e495e-a796-7cd0-26a6-611bd223463a"],
 " but POVM effects to ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurementOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "534f7e63-03c8-ee33-0175-704db662b519"],
 " (stored as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b07ad27-9e6a-154b-693c-44811b1f7f91"],
 ")."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1137775047,ExpressionUUID->"1c7a415c-3e53-b7cb-441a-5906bbe71d11"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Honest edges.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Constructors check shapes, not physics (normalization, positivity, trace \
preservation are readable but not enforced); the adjoint is the physical one \
only in orthonormal bases (Gram factors are omitted); a partial trace is \
physical only when both sides of a wire carry the same basis; ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumDistance"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "417aec05-2fbb-8238-7719-066f4a4fd102"],
 "'s default \"Fidelity\" is a distance, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "-", 
   StyleBox["Re",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["a", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["b", "TI"]]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4705486f-1ac0-4964-6d3b-62499f75184e"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->573363004,ExpressionUUID->"3af5a034-7641-6879-6a8a-3a7e03f43b43"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Placement in the literature.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " QF is read against categorical quantum mechanics (CPM construction, \
dagger-compact structure, spiders), Proto-Quipper-style circuit languages and \
operator-algebraic semantics; the claimed combination no surveyed system has \
is a basis stored with every object, three pictures connected by transforms \
(phase space unrepresented elsewhere), Stinespring channels, and a \
phase-carrying stabilizer round trip."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1565937439,ExpressionUUID->"68379bed-79e9-22be-19cc-12b77f9c7084"],

Cell["\<\
Example 15.1: the running operator, stored numbers against the represented map\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1825661031,ExpressionUUID->"460eb9f9-c41e-8ef4-6e35-30a2eda8d4de"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "PacletDirectoryLoad", 
   "[", "\"\</Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/QuantumFramework/\
QuantumFramework\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"R", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "\"\<PauliX\>\""}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
    RowBox[{"R", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
    RowBox[{"R", "[", "\"\<MatrixRepresentation\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
       " ", "\"\<PauliX\>\""}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}]}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[86]:= ",
 CellID->1952919625,ExpressionUUID->"258251be-7c16-7495-53b2-48f875a35eff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Declaring a basis turns the numbers ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35c1f832-722b-ca69-63fe-f27c07df98b3"],
 " into the operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6a50da-eb07-3910-296a-49878eb3887a"],
 "; converting the already-built ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23591dbb-79d4-ec10-5166-94e57866b77a"],
 " into its own eigenbasis gives the same stored numbers back. Applying ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "114fd905-c79d-9420-4774-d16ef229ff0a"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0047a90f-9cb0-808d-307c-4169154ad2d7"],
 " stores ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42e32fd7-26e6-6b71-7290-c6915293365b"],
 " in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a2652ed-88d4-efb2-7bde-4bb72966b598"],
 " basis, which is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0962d9db-7466-8598-3f11-d0857d10efe2"],
 " computationally:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->162062935,ExpressionUUID->"5b3d557b-19e1-b503-0ac3-4d259f951c69"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"R", "[", 
      RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
     "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"R", "[", 
       RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
      "[", "\"\<Computational\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", 
     "]"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[87]:= ",
 CellID->1483832353,ExpressionUUID->"529c5c95-0588-d8f1-02a4-55dfac22aadb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The case that makes the semantics necessary: compose ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "18bedc4a-f6ca-97e0-4845-d617837cfdca"],
 " after ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f18273e-5cf5-00f5-0527-bf78548052df"],
 ", and compare with contracting the stored numbers naively:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->421271511,ExpressionUUID->"1890d11b-851d-d227-48af-c9452ca9a10d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}], "[", "R", "]"}], 
     "[", "\"\<MatrixRepresentation\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"R", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[88]:= ",
 CellID->971430162,ExpressionUUID->"5b8be800-baff-aedd-0988-026a3e8bf427"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "QF returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "=", "(", GridBox[{
     {"0", "1"},
     {
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "0"}
    }], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "224fae0e-4768-b263-5274-406872020149"],
 "; the naive contraction gives the identity, the wrong operator. The basis \
is part of the object, and composition reconciles it before summing."
}], "Text",
 CellID->411794565,ExpressionUUID->"3d32ba1d-71ed-60b8-64c1-3c4707983282"],

Cell["\<\
Example 15.2: one family of matrices, read as a channel and as a measurement\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->211393631,ExpressionUUID->"3ccd4f42-4869-4b08-64f3-672c691c1652"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Liouvillian of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cf63df4-f608-7ba6-348d-b4b183bd498c"],
 " acting on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60948258-d69f-7f2c-10ab-2405e32a4276"],
 " is a map on density matrices stored as an operator; its output is the \
trace-zero commutator:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->485898233,ExpressionUUID->"5bf5c13c-8c81-f0bf-098a-d9662535c285"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Liouvillian\>\"", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
   "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[89]:= ",
 CellID->300459616,ExpressionUUID->"27ebc314-3813-af61-4de8-db5eb9a7f24b"],

Cell["\<\
A list read as Kraus operators is a channel (stored as a Stinespring \
isometry); a list read as effects is a POVM:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1400905077,ExpressionUUID->"59cd495b-92f8-de82-0ff3-61052772a4e8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ch", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumChannel", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ch", "[", 
      RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
     "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ch", "[", "\"\<TracePreservingQ\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"m", "[", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[90]:= ",
 CellID->900992407,ExpressionUUID->"1597811c-d04f-58d0-43ac-1959e1fa2a3a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bit-flip channel sends ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d69ae9d-d0a3-a5e3-3b16-47c6e1570fc9"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e10fbdd-fcac-b923-462f-f286f55e0809"],
 " and is trace preserving; the POVM with effects ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c26b95-e958-d351-18f1-82de88d2a1bb"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56b7d10b-4c3b-5ee0-7e4c-c95565ce24ca"],
 " gives Born probabilities ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "3", "/", "4"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "4", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40ed67f4-ffa0-5cce-7093-7eb1fa552614"],
 ". Finally, measuring the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4dc0df98-8a2c-0889-7bff-d6c22fd95ad3"],
 " observable on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2226f602-e60c-c55a-53dd-e86f93beafa0"],
 " returns branch states that are ",
 StyleBox["unnormalized", "TI"],
 ", each of norm ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ed808ee-885a-0ea1-76e7-a1c829ef548b"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1909490419,ExpressionUUID->"1627cdbb-2852-50d0-3fdc-e4e549e7223a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mx", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"R", "[", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"mx", "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
       RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
     "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"mx", "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[91]:= ",
 CellID->809304935,ExpressionUUID->"6801141d-c5dc-e96b-183e-8e46ec6ebbb1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Probabilities ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1", "/", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "2", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fb5e010-3b47-28f4-554a-fa5abef27ade"],
 " and two branch kets of norm ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69461d9a-9714-a717-1f7d-94c422a60a7d"],
 ": the branch, its probability and the conditional state are three distinct \
objects, and QF keeps them distinct."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1060035609,ExpressionUUID->"1b3cd9b2-b2f5-0832-4ac3-d0ffc6805b18"],

Cell["16. Boson Sampling Explained", "Section",
 CellID->960351252,ExpressionUUID->"17254721-59fc-dba5-3edb-5e8b5f8ea98f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Source: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"/", "Users"}], "/", "mohammadb"}], "/", "Documents"}], "/",
         "GitHub"}], "/", "QuantumFramework"}], "/", "OngoingProjects"}], "/",
      "Boson"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sampling", "/", "boson"}]}], "-", 
   RowBox[{"sampling", ".", "md"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52d6b4d2-7b23-95d3-02ed-2d9c7ed7ff39"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1269096941,ExpressionUUID->"133f88c9-4e43-c7a8-42c4-21936bf7adf2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Note for review: the essay builds every network from ",
 Cell[BoxData["BeamSplitterOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "525bf512-066b-f79b-0278-ed5cb31fdde1"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["PhaseShiftOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7020b0a8-e1ec-de26-21df-29f5979ea50c"],
 " in truncated Fock space, and Part IV concludes that QuantumFramework loses \
to plain-WL photon-sector methods by orders of magnitude with few photons in \
many modes. ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumInterferometer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f4e56ea-c348-0e14-1576-4fb7f6fd557e"],
 ", which now computes the same probabilities as permanents with no Fock \
cutoff (Topics 13, 14), does not appear; Part IV's comparison may need a QI \
column before it is shown as a statement about QF."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2008479665,ExpressionUUID->"2c7820da-3afe-8c15-5407-b984be88d77f"],

Cell["Summary", "Subsection",
 CellID->29625565,ExpressionUUID->"491026a6-dd30-329c-7f2f-bf03d4ca80e6"],

Cell["\<\
A computation-first tour from two photons on a beam splitter to the classical \
hardness of boson sampling, with every result cross-checked three ways: \
Fock-space simulation in QuantumFramework, the permanent formula, and plain \
Wolfram Language.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->9883570,ExpressionUUID->"78f9e5c0-5bc5-e73b-2886-fcaa5e71ca01"],

Cell["What should catch a physicist's attention:", "Text",
 CellID->940978275,ExpressionUUID->"295a1104-8f0a-9295-5f79-896e2abce0ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["HOM and its dip, symbolically.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The coincidence amplitude of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34e49fcf-314b-942d-5c9b-16a940ffff77"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "28081ee1-9923-6846-5837-97cb18d63aac"],
 "; with photons distinguished by a polarization angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35d104ab-d16d-b332-63ee-9df4e0191e18"],
 " the coincidence probability is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "22"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8fdcfc-c987-8804-75b4-d5b9e833db6e"],
 ", reducing at the balanced splitter to the HOM dip ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4bb02784-750c-cc73-794f-beee7cbe9759"],
 ". Photon-number conservation is checked as an exact commutator in the \
untruncated ladder-operator algebra (",
 Cell[BoxData["BosonicNormalOrder"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6368bf1a-89ab-f709-1117-3744285fda53"],
 ")."
}], "Item",
 CellID->173258875,ExpressionUUID->"18aa8291-c565-6e81-48a9-1bdaec1034eb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Truncation is physics, not bookkeeping.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0fb37437-3ad9-e813-3541-6e71bf6dbb79"],
 " photons need ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29c235d7-86a4-1a63-5ff1-ac9133516949"],
 " levels per mode; one level too few either leaks probability or, with the \
matrix-exponential construction, freezes the interference entirely (or \
invents outputs a suppression law forbids)."
}], "Item",
 CellID->792860948,ExpressionUUID->"7c4bd199-468e-1df0-2448-c8c3733b67da"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Any interferometer from beam splitters.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A Reck decomposition written as a Givens-rotation fold builds any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5faac466-18c1-c293-05a9-de40997590f9"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b2a52a2-44e1-aebb-392a-4b0c6c95f481"],
 " splitters and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "146756d1-ea39-ec02-3c1d-4f9a8fcdb768"],
 " phase shifters, symbolic entries included."
}], "Item",
 CellID->124530881,ExpressionUUID->"1a7ee52b-d767-0389-4a05-fd74e21251d3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Every probability is a permanent; fermions get the determinant.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Checked symbolically for general complex matrices, including \
multiply-occupied inputs, and for a symbolic three-splitter mesh."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1312473818,ExpressionUUID->"419fd7e1-c297-cbe2-77a4-cecaf72399c8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Suppression laws and their limits.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The Fourier tritter darkens exactly the patterns whose mode-label sum is \
not a multiple of 3 (Tichy et al.); at six photons the permanent finds dark \
patterns the law does not predict."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1627779716,ExpressionUUID->"7a33ac2f-4fb5-380e-2bc0-45896a418b54"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Bunching as a theorem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Fully bunched outputs are exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b56b9eb-04f6-5b17-696d-30b5ac83267d"],
 " times likelier for identical photons in every interferometer; the \
Haar-average bunching probability follows from Schur's lemma and matches a \
1000-sample Monte Carlo."
}], "Item",
 CellID->294107029,ExpressionUUID->"6e9dc2e4-4753-bfbd-16a2-dbce72e70587"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Where the cost lives.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The truncated Fock space ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7db41629-8d3d-b9f9-2b4b-887324c90bc3"],
 " against the photon sector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Binomial"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f51d24b-32fb-3155-656e-d415468f83bf"],
 "; two photon-sector representations (a polynomial in creation operators and \
a ",
 Cell[BoxData["SymmetrizedArray"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32e9efb5-7328-71d0-6296-06ff06dd433a"],
 " of permanents); Glynn's permanent doubling with every photon; a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1000", "\[Times]", "1000"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0aa19f46-928a-afd4-3a5e-1720273cf53e"],
 " determinant (fermions) cheaper than a 24-photon permanent."
}], "Item",
 CellID->736271930,ExpressionUUID->"31860dcc-84f8-941b-67bd-a4962d72ff61"],

Cell["\<\
Example 16.1: Hong-Ou-Mandel with partially distinguishable photons\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->406066173,ExpressionUUID->"08371d00-4cf7-24ac-39cc-956a64838ef6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Path and polarization modes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["1", 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox["1", 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e555e8f-0ad0-492d-166b-57e9af651877"],
 "; the second photon is polarized at angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "348b0551-d20e-4e96-5c88-9d1ae7bb14fc"],
 "; a non-polarizing beam splitter acts on both polarizations:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->783505316,ExpressionUUID->"5c065349-950a-8738-043e-4b131cbcea02"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "PacletDirectoryLoad", 
   "[", "\"\</Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/QuantumFramework/\
QuantumFramework\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], ";", " ", 
  
  RowBox[{
  "Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"", "]"}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"inPol", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Chi]", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Chi]", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", "3"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bsPol", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"BeamSplitterOperator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", 
        
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]}], "]"}], ",",
       "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"BeamSplitterOperator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", 
        
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
     "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"coincidence", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "@", 
    RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "@", 
     RowBox[{"Total", "@", 
      RowBox[{"KeySelect", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"KeyMap", "[", 
         RowBox[{"First", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"bsPol", "[", "inPol", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", 
           "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"#", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"#", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], " ", "&&",
           " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"#", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"#", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}]}], " ", 
         "&"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"coincidence", " ", "==", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "^", "4"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "^", "4"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Chi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", "2"}]}]}]}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "|", " ", "\[Chi]"}], ")"}], " ", "\[Element]",
       " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"coincidence", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Chi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[92]:= ",
 CellID->1838581182,ExpressionUUID->"4ff276a9-5e86-52e3-7582-6ff35b3320c9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The coincidence probability interpolates between identical photons (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "24b6e2ad-c501-b7fc-4c4d-fbf6ecb51dc6"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "22"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "230cad6b-7900-e120-5133-453578bab00a"],
 ") and classical particles (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "086f7f71-a7b7-bd3e-3815-773ad2430404"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cdf8892-1d3f-31f6-34e4-21dc94cb83dc"],
 "); at the balanced splitter it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e0217c2-6a7a-d359-2631-8eac0f0ca1a3"],
 ", the HOM dip, with the polarization overlap ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4104c6da-03d7-a765-773b-df84b6630a4f"],
 " setting its depth."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1015299810,ExpressionUUID->"731f4b84-5335-8b87-2125-62ee66c1d9ed"],

Cell["\<\
Example 16.2: permanents, suppression laws, and the n! of bunching\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->320909480,ExpressionUUID->"315717aa-70ab-e706-676c-8ef4015fca6c"],

Cell["\<\
The permanent formula for identical and distinguishable photons:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1950243504,ExpressionUUID->"7c1b1617-f81f-7a45-2438-8850f9aa48af"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "occ_List", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Catenate", "@", 
    RowBox[{"MapIndexed", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"First", "[", "#2", "]"}], ",", " ", "#1"}], "]"}], " ", 
       "&"}], ",", " ", "occ"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"bosonProbability", "[", 
    RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
       RowBox[{"w", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^",
      "2"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"s", "!"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"t", "!"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"distinguishableProbability", "[", 
    RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"w", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", 
      "2"}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"t", "!"}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "m_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ReverseSort", "@", 
    RowBox[{"FrobeniusSolve", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "m"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[93]:= ",
 CellID->1158471628,ExpressionUUID->"70b05f1a-470c-9c9d-2040-574472bee6e7"],

Cell["\<\
The tritter's dark outputs are exactly those the suppression law predicts; at \
six photons the law misses some:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->600867794,ExpressionUUID->"4a8c5b06-7c6a-07f5-7ab4-5360751f6ddf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
      RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"PossibleZeroQ", "[", 
        RowBox[{"bosonProbability", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          "#"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "===", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"!", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Divisible", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], ",", 
          " ", "3"}], "]"}]}]}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Length", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
       RowBox[{"6", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Divisible", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], ",", 
          " ", "6"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"PossibleZeroQ", "[", 
         RowBox[{"bosonProbability", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "6", "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
            RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], 
         "]"}]}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[94]:= ",
 CellID->570648126,ExpressionUUID->"4fa3f928-0446-c8dd-7550-f172adf09a27"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3727240c-f62b-7b8f-5edc-be6983de49d5"],
 ", and twelve six-photon patterns that the law allows are dark anyway: the \
law is sufficient, not necessary. For a fully general complex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"6", "\[Times]", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50637aef-2122-41f7-0011-73c950d713dd"],
 " transfer matrix, every all-in-one-mode output is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63773809-2d44-01f7-110c-b25344f153dd"],
 " times likelier for identical photons:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1943045306,ExpressionUUID->"7ede8b7e-b317-5b7c-26e5-233bc6a22646"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"w", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[FormalW]", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"6", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"n", " ", 
          RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "6", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"bosonProbability", "[", 
             RowBox[{"w", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], 
              ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "==", "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"n", "!"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"distinguishableProbability", "[", 
              RowBox[{"w", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}],
                ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[95]:= ",
 CellID->1695469705,ExpressionUUID->"75c8f24b-f46e-7672-23f7-f414fd1b5d58"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d149507-d3df-875e-5b2b-0d60e66beda4"],
 " is the number of identical-row permutations in the permanent, which the \
determinant would cancel instead: the exchange sign decides both bunching and \
computational cost."
}], "Text",
 CellID->808446663,ExpressionUUID->"772d62ae-4bf9-dab0-1ed3-7b086d8da89a"],

Cell["17. Why Boson Sampling Is Hard", "Section",
 CellID->843355028,ExpressionUUID->"7a8c9a4d-0caa-515e-2ab3-1c17a55f23a4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Source: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"/", "Users"}], "/", "mohammadb"}], "/", "Documents"}], "/",
         "GitHub"}], "/", "QuantumFramework"}], "/", "OngoingProjects"}], "/",
      "Boson"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sampling", "/", "why"}]}], "-", "boson", "-", "sampling", "-", 
   "is", "-", 
   RowBox[{"hard", ".", "md"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a4c6a75-6554-e0e6-1a73-8c3f0ce6b2cc"],
 " (has uncommitted edits; written on ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumInterferometer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29c3108e-8c9d-f317-5ff0-89e82529de7d"],
 ")."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2123001010,ExpressionUUID->"5b90d741-2df1-4c37-09af-cf2b4b84171d"],

Cell["Summary", "Subsection",
 CellID->1415208481,ExpressionUUID->"5a353f88-1ea4-a3d5-0bca-b6d29b56f13f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A compact companion to Topic 16 that keeps three tasks apart, computing one \
amplitude, collecting every probability, and drawing one sample, because the \
hardness argument lives in the gap between them. Built entirely on ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumInterferometer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c3a5085-d835-7232-65da-49eed9c04118"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->80082845,ExpressionUUID->"2f71b61d-3801-a1b0-550e-2847b9b5f39a"],

Cell["What should catch a physicist's attention:", "Text",
 CellID->730828669,ExpressionUUID->"3c7c9f19-7bfc-9bea-6403-17437d8ee930"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Three particle statistics, one table.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " On a balanced splitter, identical bosons never give a coincidence \
(permanent), distinguishable particles give ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "4"], ",", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], ",", 
   FractionBox["1", "4"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4bcd3c0f-0044-41be-79f2-b669b1f11384"],
 " (permanent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["W", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250574e2-7568-dee6-533b-6dcc7c02a4cc"],
 "), and identical fermions always give one (determinant); the minus sign in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "570dea5b-028b-2dc3-7d32-0c05b73e7729"],
 " is what cancels the bosonic coincidence."
}], "Item",
 CellID->20229285,ExpressionUUID->"559114f0-95cd-3728-03ae-8dba1c799a72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The permanent derived, not postulated.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Each input creation operator maps to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "499d2cc9-9173-f7c8-7fa2-c5932007dd12"],
 "; the output amplitudes are coefficients of the polynomial ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"],
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b3687b6-15a3-de20-4acd-1ef09c57a50a"],
 ", which is how QI's ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Probabilities\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "073f26db-34e5-c8c2-2ec4-bf85bc919a28"],
 " computes the whole distribution, checked complex amplitude by complex \
amplitude against independent permanents."
}], "Item",
 CellID->865532999,ExpressionUUID->"27056d96-6b3e-545a-4d3a-84d00ecb3ea0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cost depends on occupation structure.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In random ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "031df9cf-6b45-d275-3122-f0a90ef1a15f"],
 "-mode networks, a collision-free or paired amplitude grows exponentially \
with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79902eb9-9fc4-d4aa-2faf-c7e31a76bef0"],
 ", while a fully bunched one stays essentially free because it reduces to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubsuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], ",", "1"}], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e90dac8-e749-9c1a-16af-d39592fde760"],
 "; collision-free amplitudes reach minutes near 28-29 photons."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1719354248,ExpressionUUID->"2f026f1c-d8c2-1814-5531-8759d9776b7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Hard to compute is not hard to sample.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Distinguishable photons have permanent probabilities yet are sampled \
trivially column by column; what turns amplitude cost into sampling hardness \
is the Aaronson-Arkhipov argument (exact sampling would collapse the \
polynomial hierarchy; approximate sampling under Gaussian-permanent \
conjectures), alongside Clifford-Clifford's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox["2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c65fa9b-46f3-ebf0-041a-f3c57287b9da"],
 " exact sampler."
}], "Item",
 CellID->803807756,ExpressionUUID->"583cd303-9cb1-03ae-09c3-cb6d154451f4"],

Cell["\<\
Example 17.1: bosons, classical particles and fermions on one beam splitter\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->601042471,ExpressionUUID->"18f1bad1-a8d9-f26a-488e-339ac96dc0b0"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "PacletDirectoryLoad", 
   "[", "\"\</Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/QuantumFramework/\
QuantumFramework\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], ";", " ", 
  
  RowBox[{
  "Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"", "]"}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "occ_List", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Catenate", "@", 
    RowBox[{"MapIndexed", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"First", "[", "#2", "]"}], ",", " ", "#1"}], "]"}], " ", 
       "&"}], ",", " ", "occ"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"bosonProb", "[", 
    RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
       RowBox[{"w", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^",
      "2"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Factorial", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
       RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"distProb", "[", 
    RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "w", "]"}], "^", "2"}], ")"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Factorial", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"fermionProb", "[", 
    RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
      RowBox[{"w", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^",
     "2"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Wbs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}],
     "[", "\"\<TransferMatrix\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Through", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"bosonProb", ",", " ", "distProb", ",", " ", "fermionProb"}], 
      "}"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"Wbs", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[96]:= ",
 CellID->2038927162,ExpressionUUID->"6cd8e50a-7117-62ea-14e7-fd5400a23030"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Rows are the outputs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"2,0"},
    "Ket"], ",", 
   TemplateBox[{"1,1"},
    "Ket"], ",", 
   TemplateBox[{"0,2"},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b9c4f1f-9707-8ca1-29a4-675922b3d68b"],
 "; columns are identical bosons, distinguishable particles and identical \
fermions. Bosons bunch (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], ",", "0", ",", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0839f778-d15e-09ff-39c6-ef25e0eb5bc5"],
 "), classical particles split (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "4"], ",", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], ",", 
   FractionBox["1", "4"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7962e333-0c57-77b8-2f11-fb7da5e25d82"],
 "), fermions antibunch (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e58b71a-bb3b-e382-3667-2f443ecfb1e8"],
 "): the only difference is the sign attached to exchanging two histories."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1188205371,ExpressionUUID->"7517e465-645e-477c-232c-fe4f0deb2a46"],

Cell["\<\
Example 17.2: what one amplitude costs, and why structure matters\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1003860385,ExpressionUUID->"560e68d9-da1a-2272-7e35-8182dfaf7158"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Collision-free, paired and fully bunched inputs in random networks with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46aa8ea3-37c3-4040-6ea9-270d427612aa"],
 " modes, one QI amplitude each:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->952137231,ExpressionUUID->"6acb7fb5-f6da-6094-1ac9-76fe836f32fe"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"occupations", "[", "n_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
      RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"<|", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<collision-free\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<pairs\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
          RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Quotient", "[", 
            RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Mod", "[", 
          RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<bunched\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "n", "}"}]}]}], "|>"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"randomInterferometer", "[", "n_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
      RowBox[{"1107", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1000", " ", "n"}]}], "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Random\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"timeAmplitude", "[", 
    RowBox[{"q_", ",", " ", "s_List"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"RotateRight", "[", 
        RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Total", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ClearSystemCache", "[", "]"}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"First", "@", 
       RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", 
        RowBox[{"q", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"s", " ", "->", " ", "t"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"q", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"randomInterferometer", "[", "n", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"timeAmplitude", "[", 
          RowBox[{"q", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"occupations", "[", "n", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"6", ",", " ", "12", ",", " ", "18", ",", " ", "20"}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[97]:= ",
 CellID->1052272830,ExpressionUUID->"7a5ec95d-e220-f105-2a65-e10697dac06f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "From 12 to 20 photons the collision-free and paired amplitudes grow by more \
than two orders of magnitude, while the fully bunched one barely moves: a \
generic permanent pays the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05590d03-2064-1772-3366-a56d51117a58"],
 " of Ryser and Glynn, a structured one does not. That is why worst-case \
#P-hardness is a statement about generic instances, and why the \
sampling-hardness argument needs random networks."
}], "Text",
 CellID->775731387,ExpressionUUID->"3b9b9f37-eb8f-88a6-69b8-17708e3bda8c"]
},
